      ],
      "source": "https://floridahistoryblog.com/cities/forest-city/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Forest City developed as a central citrus production hub and was home to Forest Lake Academy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://floridahistoryblog.com/cities/forest-city/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The old Orange Belt Railroad line once ran through Forest City and is now partially a bike trail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://floridahistoryblog.com/cities/forest-city/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Soldiers once navigated the sawgrass and shimmering lakes of Forest City to protect settlers from conflict.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://explory.world/poi/forest-city/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Forest City is located in the southwestern corner of Seminole County, between Apopka and Altamonte Springs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://floridahistoryblog.com/cities/forest-city/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Forest City reflects the evolution of Florida from an untamed frontier to a place where history and progress converge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
